{SECT 0 {EXCHG {PARA 18 "" 0 "" {TEXT 280 15 "Assignment Five" }}
{PARA 19 "" 0 "" {TEXT 281 14 "Rachel Prather" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 
"" {TEXT 212 11 " Problem 1." }{TEXT 282 3 "   " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT 282 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 282 44 "Generate 8 random 3 by \+
3 matrices using the " }{TEXT 213 12 "RandomMatrix" }{TEXT 282 19 " co
mmand from the  " }{TEXT 214 13 "LinearAlgebra" }{TEXT 282 42 " packag
e. As each matrix is generated use " }{TEXT 215 11 "Eigenvalues" }
{TEXT 282 160 " to compute its eigenvalues. Then take the product of t
he eigenvalues, and check that for each matrix, this product is equal \+
to the determinant of the matrix.  " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 282 0 "" 
}}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 282 1 "[" }{TEXT 216 6 "Hint: " }{TEXT 282 79 
"The product will be complicated algebraically and you will need to ap
ply first " }{TEXT 217 6 "expand" }{TEXT 282 7 ", then " }{TEXT 218 8 
"simplify" }{TEXT 282 132 " to reduce the product of the eigenvalues t
o an integer. First try to do for a single matrix , then make a loop t
o do it 8 times.]  " }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 8 "resta
rt:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 20 "with(LinearAlgebra);
